{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 10253159633609905675, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 639, "mtime": 1791872379.9689026, "sha256": "dae5e0ec1e1693f758c13fe280cf45ac8548f3152782fe0dd2142ac549ebe9f6"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 524, "mtime": 1791872383.6890168, "sha256": "57214fb2a5d8384b46f314ab27e5f1c568997e93adff0208bfef8cff71f8ed57"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/29/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/29/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Now a regression test, then run it.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** Python stores `2.675` as `2.67499999\u2026` in binary, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round()` also rounds halves to the nearest even digit, not up as the docstring says, so `0.125` gave `0.12`.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now converts `str(x)` (the shortest form, `\"2.675\"`) to a `Decimal` and rounds it with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It still returns a `float`, so `add_vat` and any other callers don't need to change. Negative halves now round away from zero: `-2.675` gives `-2.68`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`. pytest isn't installed here, so neither test file has been run through pytest. I ran the same cases directly with `python3` and all passed:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `2.675` | `2.68` |\n| `0.125` | `0.13` |\n| `1.005` | `1.01` |\n| `2.674` | `2.67` |\n| `-2.675` | `-2.68` |\n| `3` | `3.0` |\n| `add_vat(10.0)` | `12.0` |\n\nThe existing `test_split` also still passes.\n\n**Limitation:** the result depends on Python's shortest form of the float. If arithmetic upstream lands just below a half, e.g. `1.0049999999999999`, it rounds down. Fixing that would mean keeping prices as `Decimal` or as integer cents all the way through, which is a bigger change than this fix.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 274435, "requests_cache_write": 15138, "requests_cost_usd": 0.186085, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2771, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial29", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 56, "score": 1.0, "sta